## 🔐 Relevance to Security Awareness Training
When employees connect their corporate laptops to public airport or hotel Wi-Fi, they often assume their web traffic is invisible. In this project, I used Wireshark to literally pull DNS requests out of thin air, showing exactly which websites a machine is asking to visit. When I train staff on the mandatory use of corporate VPNs, I don't just tell them "it encrypts your data"—I show them this exact packet capture. Seeing their computer broadcast "Where is facebook.com?" or "Where is the corporate payroll portal?" in cleartext across the network makes the abstract concept of eavesdropping immediately real. It makes the abstract threat of eavesdropping immediately visible — and gives employees a concrete reason to trust the VPN policy rather than resent it.

